# 1. The perfect WhatsApp response architecture

## Do not make the webhook wait for the whole answer

The webhook path must be divided into two phases:

```text
Phase A — acknowledge quickly
receive webhook
verify signature
deduplicate event
persist minimal event
return HTTP 200

Phase B — process asynchronously
interpret message
query database
call AI if required
send WhatsApp reply
record delivery state
```

The webhook should not wait for:

- an LLM response;
- OCR or menu extraction;
- a long database workflow;
- payment-provider reconciliation;
- driver routing;
- campaign audience generation;
- a human support lookup.

The customer’s first acknowledgement should be sent through a fast deterministic path whenever possible:

> One moment — I’m checking that for you.

Use this only when the actual answer will take longer than the target. Do not send unnecessary filler for every tap.

## Fast path versus slow path

Every inbound event should be classified immediately:

```text
interactive button/list tap → fast deterministic path
STOP/privacy command → fast deterministic path
cart quantity/edit → fast deterministic path
order status → fast deterministic path
location pin → fast deterministic path
simple menu search → deterministic path
ambiguous natural language → one model call
voice note → asynchronous transcription path
menu upload → asynchronous extraction job
complaint/refund/allergy → human-safe slower path
```

The fast path must not initialize an AI client, load large prompts, or query unnecessary tables.

