# 7. Search and menu caching

## Menu read model

For a menu page, return one compact payload:

```json
{
  "vendor": {
    "id": "...",
    "name": "...",
    "currency": "USD",
    "is_open": true,
    "menu_version": 12
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "...",
      "name": "Shawarma",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "...",
          "name": "Chicken Shawarma",
          "price_usd": 6,
          "available": true,
          "has_options": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next_cursor": null
}
```

Do not make the WhatsApp handler separately query vendor, sections, items, options, images, and availability for each screen.

## Search strategy

Use a layered search path:

```text
exact button/item ID
→ normalized keyword search
→ Arabic/English/Arabizi alias search
→ structured cuisine/zone filters
→ vector similarity only when needed
→ AI only for genuine ambiguity
```

Cache deterministic search results briefly by normalized query and menu version.

Do not cache a search result without including menu/version and zone context.

