# 8. AI latency and cost control

## Route by difficulty

```text
STOP/privacy/order status/button/cart → no model
simple known item or restaurant search → no model
minor typo/Arabic alias → deterministic normalization first
ambiguous request → one fast model call
complex recommendation → one capable model call
complaint/refund/allergy → safe model + human path
voice/menu upload → asynchronous job
```

## Cache AI results carefully

### Safe candidates

- translation of a stable menu item description;
- normalized search alias;
- classification of a repeated non-sensitive intent;
- menu extraction draft for the same immutable file hash;
- embeddings for an unchanged menu version;
- recommendation candidates for the same customer/menu version/time bucket where privacy rules allow.

### Do not blindly cache

- customer-specific order decisions;
- payment decisions;
- current stock claims;
- customer consent;
- allergy safety conclusions;
- real-time delivery ETA;
- support decisions that depend on current state.

## Cache key design

Include:

```text
provider
model
prompt_version
tool_schema_version
language
menu_version
customer-preference version, where appropriate
input hash
```

Example:

```text
ai:normalize-search:v3:ar:menu-192:sha256(...)
```

Never use raw customer phone numbers as cache keys.

## Prompt caching and context reduction

Reduce model cost by:

- sending only the relevant menu section;
- sending only the current basket;
- sending a compact customer preference summary;
- not sending the entire conversation every turn;
- storing a rolling summary instead of full history;
- keeping tool descriptions concise;
- using structured outputs;
- using smaller output limits;
- reusing stable prompt prefixes where the provider supports prompt caching.

Do not include full database rows or raw webhook payloads in the model context.

## Model budget policy

Set per-turn budgets:

```text
max_model_calls: 1 for ordinary text
max_model_calls: 2 for complex support
max_model_time_ms: 3500–5000
max_input_tokens: route-specific
max_output_tokens: route-specific
max_cost_usd_per_turn
```

If the limit is reached:

```text
use deterministic fallback
ask one concise clarification
or hand off to a person
```

## AI result reuse

Cache AI work only when the input facts are stable. Invalidate when:

- menu version changes;
- item availability changes;
- customer preference version changes;
- prompt version changes;
- model changes;
- campaign rules change.

