# 9. API-cost control beyond caching

## Avoid unnecessary outbound calls

For each provider, record:

```text
provider
endpoint
purpose
call count
latency
success rate
cost
cache hit/miss
retry count
```

Use request coalescing so simultaneous requests for the same data share one in-flight request.

## Batch where safe

Batch:

- menu embeddings;
- analytics events;
- driver location writes;
- settlement reconciliation;
- merchant daily reports.

Do not batch interactive customer replies where it increases perceived latency.

## Use webhooks instead of polling

Use provider webhooks for:

- WhatsApp message status;
- payment status;
- driver/dispatch events where available;
- provider reconciliation.

Use polling only as a bounded reconciliation fallback.

## Backoff and dead letters

Every external call should have:

```text
short timeout
bounded retries
exponential backoff
idempotency key
failure classification
dead-letter record
manual replay path
```

Never retry a customer-facing send forever.

## Regional placement

Keep high-frequency synchronous calls in the same or nearby region:

```text
WhatsApp/Kapso webhook worker
Supabase database
queue worker
cache
```

Accept small cross-region latency for low-frequency model calls if the overall response remains inside target.

