# 10. WhatsApp message design for speed

## Send one useful message

Follow the existing rule:

```text
one rich message per turn where possible
```

Avoid sending:

```text
“Checking…”
then “I found…”
then a card
```

unless the work truly crosses the response target.

## Fast interactive replies

Button taps should:

- use opaque IDs;
- avoid model calls;
- query one read model/RPC;
- perform one mutation if needed;
- send one response;
- enqueue non-essential analytics in the background.

Do not wait for:

- read receipts;
- analytics;
- recommendation scoring;
- full conversation summarization;
- non-critical audit enrichment.

## Voice and media

Reply quickly:

> I received your voice note and I’m checking it now.

Then process asynchronously. Do not hold the WhatsApp webhook open while transcribing or analyzing a long file.

