# Final decision

The biggest current latency problem is not that Claude or OpenAI is inherently slow. The measured system bottleneck is mainly:

```text
Kapso buffering
+ cross-region database calls
+ too many database round trips
+ too many model calls
```

Fix those in that order.

The perfect day-one database is not the most complicated database. It is:

```text
normalized for integrity
read-modeled for hot paths
indexed from real query plans
transactional for money and orders
protected by RLS
observable by default
```

The perfect cache is not a cache of everything. It is:

```text
short-lived
versioned
invalidated on merchant changes
used only for safe reads
never authoritative for money or order state
```

The best cost strategy is:

```text
zero-model deterministic flows
one model call for ordinary ambiguity
compact context
cached stable AI work
batched background work
webhooks instead of polling
strict budgets
```

If Alo King implements these foundations before scaling, it can deliver fast WhatsApp replies, lower AI/API costs, and a much more reliable customer and merchant experience.
